-- title:
--   Elements of the Fuchsian group come from norm-one units
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b$ be non-zero rationals and let $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be the associated quaternion algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ satisfying `IsOrder`, that is: $1 \in R$, $R$ is closed under multiplication, the $\mathbb{Q}$-span of $R$ is the whole algebra, and $R$ is finitely generated as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module. Let $\iota : \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \to M_2(\mathbb{R})$ be an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra homomorphism, and let $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ lie in `fuchsianGroup R ι`, i.e. in the intersection of the image of `unitGroup R` under the map induced by $\iota$ on unit groups with the kernel of the determinant homomorphism $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R}) \to \mathbb{R}^\times$; here `unitGroup R` is the subgroup of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]^\times$ generated by those units $u$ with `IsUnitOf R u`, meaning $u \in R$ and there is $v \in R$ with $uv = vu = 1$. The conclusion is that there exists $u \in \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ with $u \in R$ admitting a two-sided inverse inside $R$, whose reduced norm $\mathrm{nrd}(u) = u_{\mathrm{re}}^2 - a\,u_I^2 - b\,u_J^2 + ab\,u_K^2$ equals $1$, and such that the matrix underlying $\gamma$ is $\iota(u)$.
--
--   This identifies the Fuchsian group attached to an order $R$ and a real embedding $\iota$ with the image $\iota(R^1)$ of the norm-one units of $R$: membership in the group generated by the $R$-units, cut by $\det = 1$, already forces the representing quaternion to be an $R$-unit of reduced norm one. It is used whenever a relation between matrices in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ has to be read back as a relation between quaternions, for instance in the study of the associated Shimura curve and of fake elliptic curves with quaternionic multiplication.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_exists_isUnitOf_nrd_eq_one_of_mem_fuchsianGroup.lean

